  "body": "1,748m2 of THAB(Terraced Houses and Apartment Buildings) Zoned Land, over three Freehold Titles with three well maintained houses, on the Flat in Milford, beside Lake Pupuke\r\n\r\nThis is a high demand residential area that will produce a liquid and bankable development opportunity offering substantial yield, which will qualify for golden visa application while holding\r\n\r\no\t19 Otakau Road – \t523 sqm Fee Simple, 3 bed, 1 bath\r\no\t19A Otakau Road – \t541 sqm Fee Simple, 2 bed, 1 bath\r\no\t21 Otakau Road – \t683sqm Fee Simple, 4 bed, 2 bath\r\n\r\nMilford is a highly desirable leading North Shore Town Centre enhanced by beach and Lake, with a modern Shopping Centre, all easily accessible on level walking, only 9 minutes by bus or car from Auckland City. \r\n\r\nOtakau Road is in the heart of this premium location, a quiet cul-de-sac 300 meters safe flat walk from Milford Town Centre, cafes, churches, shops, schools, services, and close to North Shore Hospital.\r\n\r\nThe subject properties are on the flat right beside Lake Pupuke and have a north-west facing rear aspect, drenched in all day sun. \r\n\r\n•\tPotential for a substantial rate of return with either High Rise Apartments, Stand Alone or Terraced Houses.\r\n\r\n•\tTHAB zoning allows 6 story with 22 meter Allowable Build Height as notified under PC120. Zoned THAB under NPS-UD section 3d. When operable zoning allows 50% site coverage, and non notified resource consent(i.e. if you build within the building standards, neighbors consent not required)\r\n\r\n•\tAllowable build height of 22 meters, with setback/Hight in Relation to Boundary of 20 meters + 60 degrees (i.e. full height 1 meter from side boundary, and 1.5 meter from street), will produce 6 story development subject to resource consent, with lake, sea, and city views from 3 stories and above. \r\n\r\n•\tThis flat rectangular block of land when developed will require less structural build costs, resulting in a higher yield per m2\r\n\r\n•\tNo character overlays, No special interest overlays, No scheduled trees’, No flood plan overlay, and No water constraints, making this a very clean site.\r\n\r\n•\tSurveys, waste and storm water solutions engineered, along with Geotec info and potential concept plans available.\r\n\r\n•\t3 well maintained houses on 3 separate freehold titles offering desirable rental housing with strong holding income\r\n\r\nAll 3 properties available as one block, \r\n\r\nInformation pack and engineers reports available on request, viewing by appointment\r\n\r\nPhone owner on (09) 486 7799 or (027) 486 7799",
